        "original_id": "e1f89637-a7eb-54f2-b896-e27644c654b6",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Harry Craft\n- Places: Ellisville, Mississippi; Jones County, Mississippi; Laurel-Hattiesburg area\n- Organizations: Cincinnati Reds\n- Products: WJKX\n\nFacts:\n- Harry Craft was born on April 19, 1915, in Ellisville, Mississippi.\n- Harry Craft was an American Major League Baseball player and manager.\n- Harry Craft was a center fielder for the Cincinnati Reds from 1937 to 1942.\n- Ellisville is a city in Jones County, Mississippi, and it was the first county seat of Jones County.\n- Ellisville had a population of 4,448 in the 2010 census.\n- WJKX is a radio station at 102.5 FM licensed to Ellisville, Mississippi, and it serves the Laurel-Hattiesburg area.\n- Harry Craft died on August 3, 1995.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
